{"name":"Sour Veil","hex":"#ffffbf","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tasting of acidity.","Made rancid by fermentation, etc."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sensation of a sour taste.","A drink made with whiskey, lemon or lime juice and sugar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sour"},{"term":"veil","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something hung up or spread out to hide or protect the face, or hide an object from view; usually of gauze, crepe, or similar diaphanous material.","Anything that partially obscures a clear view."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To dress in, or decorate with, a veil.","To conceal as with a veil."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/veil"}],"entries":[{"title":"Veil","blocks":[{"text":"A veil is an article of clothing or hanging cloth that is intended to cover some part of the head or face, or an object of some significance. Veiling has a long history in European, Asian, and African societies. The practice has been prominent in different forms in Judaism, Christianity, and Islam. The practice of veiling is especially associated with women and sacred objects, though in some cultures, it is men, rather than women, who are expected to wear a veil. Besides its enduring religious significance, veiling continues to play a role in some modern secular contexts, such as wedding customs."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7b/Chief_Vestal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Veil"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7b/Chief_Vestal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7b/Chief_Vestal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Roman statue of a veiled Vestal Virgin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChief_Vestal.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Bronze_Statuette_of_a_Veiled_and_Masked_Dancer_1.jpg/500px-Bronze_Statuette_of_a_Veiled_and_Masked_Dancer_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Bronze_Statuette_of_a_Veiled_and_Masked_Dancer_1.jpg/500px-Bronze_Statuette_of_a_Veiled_and_Masked_Dancer_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Greek bronze statuette of a veiled and masked dancer, 2nd–3rd century BC.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABronze_Statuette_of_a_Veiled_and_Masked_Dancer_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Veils_bavaria_ncd_2012.jpg/500px-Veils_bavaria_ncd_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Veils_bavaria_ncd_2012.jpg/500px-Veils_bavaria_ncd_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Depiction of Isabeau of Bavaria, queen of France, wearing veiling","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVeils_bavaria_ncd_2012.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/A_Coptic_woman_of_the_Poorer_Class._%281918%29_-_TIMEA.jpg/500px-A_Coptic_woman_of_the_Poorer_Class._%281918%29_-_TIMEA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/A_Coptic_woman_of_the_Poorer_Class._%281918%29_-_TIMEA.jpg/500px-A_Coptic_woman_of_the_Poorer_Class._%281918%29_-_TIMEA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Coptic woman wearing a veil (1918)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_Coptic_woman_of_the_Poorer_Class._(1918)_-_TIMEA.jpg"},{